#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298885 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f87bc14d-5e68-5a5e-bec8-f1b5b21c02e8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Arc Length of a Smooth Curve Using the Arc Length Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82e29027-cd8f-5288-ad2d-035977d9cb75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}+\\ln(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82e29027-cd8f-5288-ad2d-035977d9cb75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}+\\ln(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298887} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0d4249a-3912-5dc4-871a-c97b49be5238" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1e883a7d-82a7-5e23-83d2-65862f5b051d" :question/math-academy-id "q-353183" :question/problem "Compute the arc length of $y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)$ for $x\\in [1,2].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x),$ $a=1,$ and $b=2.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{1}{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}+16}{16{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{({x}^{2}+4)^{2}}{16{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}$ into the arc length formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{{2}^{2}}{8}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2]-[\\frac{{1}^{2}}{8}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡1] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
